What mlmf derives from them, and where:

- `crates/mlmf-ggml/tests/ggml-types.tsv` and `crates/mlmf-ggml/src/types.rs`
  — ggml's type codes and block geometry (elements/block, bytes/block,
  alignment), measured from `ggml-org/llama.cpp` commit
  `9d57ce456c94d241dde672b2db9cf18879766568`: `ggml/include/ggml.h` (codes),
  `ggml/src/ggml.c` (elements/block), `ggml/src/ggml-common.h`
  (bytes/block, alignment). Facts about the format, not transcribed source
  code; cross-checked against the upstream static asserts at that commit.
- `crates/mlmf-gguf/src/requirements.rs` — GGUF's required-key table and the
  spec's own legend for "required", quoted from `ggml-org/ggml`
  `docs/gguf.md` (read 2026-09-05).
- `crates/mlmf-gguf/src/header.rs` — version-support table from
  `docs/gguf.md`'s `## Version History` (same read), and a byte-swap
  detection heuristic that has no corresponding spec section and is
  `ggml-org/llama.cpp`'s own, pinned at commit
  `9d57ce456c94d241dde672b2db9cf18879766568`, `ggml/src/gguf.cpp:497`.

No source code from either repository is copied or reproduced; these are
facts about file formats and short, attributed spec quotations.


================================================================================
unsloth/Qwen3-0.6B-unsloth-bnb-4bit and Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B (test fixture)
================================================================================

`crates/mlmf-conformance/tests/fixtures/bnb_double_quant/
bnb_double_quant_k_proj_16rows.safetensors` is real bitsandbytes NF4
double-quantization output: the first 16 rows (of 1024) of
`model.layers.1.self_attn.k_proj` from `unsloth/Qwen3-0.6B-unsloth-bnb-4bit`,
`model.safetensors`, revision `e86f5289a2ca40ab7114071959dc2079cf97cb3c`, with
the `quant_state` JSON's `shape` patched to the 16-row slice. The weights are
`Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B`'s (revision `c1899de289a04d12100db370d81485cdf75e47ca`).
Both repositories declare the licence Apache-2.0; the licence text, as
`Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B` serves it, is `crates/mlmf-conformance/tests/fixtures/
bnb_double_quant/LICENSE-Qwen3-0.6B-Apache-2.0.txt`. The fixture reached this
repository through Fuel's repository, which cut it (provenance there: 
`fuel-tensor/tests/fixtures/bnb_double_quant/PROVENANCE.md`); its blob sha256
is `1d6b7975dada0c24563ad630e944d7677714d40074c962ff462e31042026e971`, and
its five weight-bearing tensors were re-read from the real checkpoint by HTTP
range requests on 2026-10-25 and found byte-identical to the hub's. It is used
only by `crates/mlmf-conformance/tests/bnb_fixture.rs`.

================================================================================
huggingface/candle (lineage of the pickle reader)
================================================================================

The opcode set and the `_rebuild_tensor_v2` reading in `crates/mlmf-pickle`
follow the minimal pickle reader in Fuel's `fuel-formats/src/pickle.rs`, which
derives from `candle-core/src/pickle.rs` in `huggingface/candle`. candle is
licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0 (its `LICENSE-MIT` and `LICENSE-APACHE`; the GitHub
licence API reports Apache-2.0 for the repository, checked 2026-10-25).
`mlmf-pickle` is a rewrite, not a copy: objects live in an arena, every length
is bounded, and the callable allowlist is new. No candle source is reproduced.

